<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Audio on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/audio/</link><description>Recent content in Audio on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Jan 2009 16:11:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/audio/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Dial Up Modem, sound no longer heard?</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dial-up-modem-sound-no-longer-heard/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 Jan 2009 16:11:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dial-up-modem-sound-no-longer-heard/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;One sound you don&amp;rsquo;t hear very often these days, you&amp;rsquo;d to be something of a comforting sound back in the early days of the interwebs. Maybe its like a white noise machine or something.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/eKOUEpQ8pRY&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;param name="allowscriptaccess" value="always"&gt;&lt;/param&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/eKOUEpQ8pRY&amp;hl=en&amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowscriptaccess="always" allowfullscreen="true" width="425" height="344"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>10 of the Best Songbird Add-ons</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10-of-best-songbird-add-ons/</link><pubDate>Fri, 05 Dec 2008 12:01:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10-of-best-songbird-add-ons/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 23 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 50 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Is SongBird the way to go? &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base13219848"&gt; &lt;table id="table13219848" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" bgcolor="#bde0ed"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;a href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/"&gt;&lt;img src="http://creativecommons.org/images/public/somerights20.gif" alt="Some Rights Reserved" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;   &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.junauza.com/"&gt;&lt;b&gt;TECH SOURCE FROM BOHOL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Source for technology hacks, insights, tutorials, news, reviews and more... &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items13219848" style="display:block; position:block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: TECH SOURCE FROM BOHOL" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/SimplyJun/~3/473700054/10-of-best-songbird-add-ons.html"&gt;10 of the Best Songbird Add-ons&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; By noreply@blogger.com (jun auza) on free/open-source &lt;p&gt; &lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg7b463u8IjTSmajUK1CRyI3HWUj2tNheMi7B31KO4LaX8aNmoGiM_42xRBQk-6WLBp-QMGN0KXmSS-aaFDB252XvZm3n4Uw-At-hrPulHcqdQfyYh2Qh5yzDI77uBMIba5UmVrkOR0gmw/s1600-h/pot-o-gold.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px 10px 10px 0px; float: left; cursor: pointer; width: 217px; height: 320px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg7b463u8IjTSmajUK1CRyI3HWUj2tNheMi7B31KO4LaX8aNmoGiM_42xRBQk-6WLBp-QMGN0KXmSS-aaFDB252XvZm3n4Uw-At-hrPulHcqdQfyYh2Qh5yzDI77uBMIba5UmVrkOR0gmw/s320/pot-o-gold.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;The first stable version of Songbird has been unleashed. Considered by many as the Firefox of media players due to its extensibility, this open source &lt;a href="http://www.junauza.com/2008/09/5-great-itunes-replacements-for.html" target="Bwindow"&gt;iTunes replacement&lt;/a&gt; has a bright future ahead.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;I had a good time with &lt;a href="http://www.junauza.com/2008/09/songbird-rocks.html" target="Bwindow"&gt;Songbird&lt;/a&gt; Beta so my expectations are high for version 1.0.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;One of the very first things to do after installing Songbird is to get and test-drive some of the available extensions. At the moment, there are probably hundreds of add-ons, so as a guide to new Songbird users, let me share to you a few of my favorites:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;1. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;LyricMaster&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;The name says it all. This add-on will help you fetch lyrics the easy way. Here are some of its important features:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;* Ability to edit the lyrics&lt;br /&gt;* Fetch the lyrics for one or more songs at a time&lt;br /&gt;* Displays the lyrics a song has embedded through metadata&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;I always want to sing along with my favorite songs so I have this installed :-)&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg8PePVHHP6Ahn-dd69_zIXH3A7iWyFPYsgq07gEynzgHEnMw0ZGwiLSpAcx_flFGucdXYro28Qw9W1efdo9TzNRl21HMO5Ypx9izDTDRzNdGLsPpWf2R5ihxHswjSxtNasoGTpqN0EtQ4/s1600-h/lm_screen01_large.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 230px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg8PePVHHP6Ahn-dd69_zIXH3A7iWyFPYsgq07gEynzgHEnMw0ZGwiLSpAcx_flFGucdXYro28Qw9W1efdo9TzNRl21HMO5Ypx9izDTDRzNdGLsPpWf2R5ihxHswjSxtNasoGTpqN0EtQ4/s320/lm_screen01_large.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Download LyricMaster &lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;a style="font-weight: bold;" href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/1230/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;HERE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;2. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Goose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Since I'm obsessed with speed, I really love this extremely lightweight Songbird feather (theme). If you are running Songbird in an ultra low-end PC, then installing this theme should help make things a little bit faster.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiDe7IOSyl43NwajeF11BuYdm_a9ThtL3iMT22zZ8iBbB23k8LmTVhQCs8hLmuqA5NtQDisznOMSMrjz15oyS7PI1EO5X5a9MJF-0LPcSfjdws3fBJSU-c0IwCIwMcvFJPFxhvNQupzq5A/s1600-h/Goose054_large.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 231px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiDe7IOSyl43NwajeF11BuYdm_a9ThtL3iMT22zZ8iBbB23k8LmTVhQCs8hLmuqA5NtQDisznOMSMrjz15oyS7PI1EO5X5a9MJF-0LPcSfjdws3fBJSU-c0IwCIwMcvFJPFxhvNQupzq5A/s320/Goose054_large.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Download Goose &lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/82/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;3. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Wikipedia Extension&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;This add-on should come in handy if you want to check out information of the song's artist. The Wikipedia entry is by default displayed at the bottom content pane.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEi-tcH2pxkURQnM_bLU-Vj0T0R-GJ-4-1LsCnfhYwPFmfucMFhLQjV6w7htAynzQFoBCPSTfcLLSn9YQbaBx1CtPe35FdwsQOBPElxtoaqhSqhD66S2ieiw8xV13atOYyFuhnHUfGVgVKk/s1600-h/wiki.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 236px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEi-tcH2pxkURQnM_bLU-Vj0T0R-GJ-4-1LsCnfhYwPFmfucMFhLQjV6w7htAynzQFoBCPSTfcLLSn9YQbaBx1CtPe35FdwsQOBPElxtoaqhSqhD66S2ieiw8xV13atOYyFuhnHUfGVgVKk/s320/wiki.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Download Wikipedia Extension &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/82/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;4. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;iPod Device Support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;This is a must-have extension for iPod owners, as this will give Songbird the ability to sync songs from its media library to the iPod. Once the iPod is mounted, you will also be able to play songs from the device playlist.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhQU7QzGsoTwF9lK2zDkOI4RWrekR6q2WEF2uoaWq6L423nrvsiXcFJg9b_7J34d4-3F0hQaM6uqGX9mvBEx1HLKVMUCirA3KDNeGhBa6qFlv4uQjdFlLUj7bsTUiZRe6ChX90zxQXBI4Q/s1600-h/ipod-screenshot_large.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 240px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhQU7QzGsoTwF9lK2zDkOI4RWrekR6q2WEF2uoaWq6L423nrvsiXcFJg9b_7J34d4-3F0hQaM6uqGX9mvBEx1HLKVMUCirA3KDNeGhBa6qFlv4uQjdFlLUj7bsTUiZRe6ChX90zxQXBI4Q/s320/ipod-screenshot_large.jpg" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Download iPod Device Support &lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;a style="font-weight: bold;" href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/12/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;HERE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;5. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;The Exorcist &lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Formerly called Ghostbusters, this extension will give Songbird some useful features. Two media views namely Ghost Tracks and Duplicate Tracks will show all the broken/missing tracks and duplicate tracks so that you can easily delete them if you want to.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgWSuApI4dI9BUCPrgBLoyKkDiUc1z4pB5xq0KlPJjVI8_WB3csHaM3u4UXvH5Zv3XvLvsTwtvAMDitjsFQ6hyphenhyphenyXSen50b0PjK9zhqCgmz1_JGH9dS1WZ7ccHc5AVAwcwZjmm6AbAnrmMo/s1600-h/ghost.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgWSuApI4dI9BUCPrgBLoyKkDiUc1z4pB5xq0KlPJjVI8_WB3csHaM3u4UXvH5Zv3XvLvsTwtvAMDitjsFQ6hyphenhyphenyXSen50b0PjK9zhqCgmz1_JGH9dS1WZ7ccHc5AVAwcwZjmm6AbAnrmMo/s320/ghost.jpg" alt="" style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 99px;" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download The Exorcist &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/216/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;6. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Last.fm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Keep your Last.fm profile up-to-date with what you've been listening to on your computer through Songbird. If you're playing music offline, the Songbird Last.fm add-on will post what you played when you come back online.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiCJZHAHqjjqtNo5luuzZKTeRTvx3_zI7bv0PwrZFfHqCI34-YS37AF2YrHzqzU7tUb6QMUmzdQqLAZYG1dMcDmggWbiJqon0_31v8o2gUNbHfHGNMECWExahAoeraT9ieh-ynpBCT4zu0/s1600-h/lastfm-screenshot_large.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiCJZHAHqjjqtNo5luuzZKTeRTvx3_zI7bv0PwrZFfHqCI34-YS37AF2YrHzqzU7tUb6QMUmzdQqLAZYG1dMcDmggWbiJqon0_31v8o2gUNbHfHGNMECWExahAoeraT9ieh-ynpBCT4zu0/s320/lastfm-screenshot_large.jpg" alt="" style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 300px; height: 225px;" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download Last.fm &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/106/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;7. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Ububird&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;Ubuntu-inspired sleek and brownish Songbird feather that will blend with Ubuntu's default desktop theme.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhSw5jK6IPx_czxLiu8KCLt7bcaYv2ECyWJfaM6moU0xcWNVPAF_xlibI3EgI7l9WFsMFaQd_XCAKfCbQPX73tpKy5s0FAUezq6JEHi__ZdSGzykjZmuh_srasZJZq8j6mFTHLPXkonSRI/s1600-h/Ubuntu.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhSw5jK6IPx_czxLiu8KCLt7bcaYv2ECyWJfaM6moU0xcWNVPAF_xlibI3EgI7l9WFsMFaQd_XCAKfCbQPX73tpKy5s0FAUezq6JEHi__ZdSGzykjZmuh_srasZJZq8j6mFTHLPXkonSRI/s320/Ubuntu.jpg" alt="" style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 231px;" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download Ububird &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/109/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;8. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;iTunes Library Importer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;This will be really useful if you have an existing iTunes library that you want to import to Songbird.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;The iTunes importer may be used on Linux to import an iTunes library from Mac or Windows. However, the file paths in the iTunes library file must be modified first. For example, a global change such as changing "D:" to "mnt/data" would allow an import of files that were stored on a Windows "D:" drive and mounted on a Linux "/mnt/data" drive.&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download iTunes Library Importer &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/9/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;9. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;Now Playing List&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;This extension should have been included by default in Songbird. It allows you to queue up songs from the library into a collapsible pane on the right, and then play them as a playlist. You can also save the list as a playlist if you like.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhWh2mymdeikIYNEF5tQ9etKdlbsN1tJpDqpyph1TKovoHyS8dwcEhBTY6ppNDdnd4Ls6kjhlGq8oXOLqWtFNfI2bpBR-hHWmk97V1tMtly-eWsmgZ5EjZr8Bd8xZ1rMdoPgL3fhOufZU4/s1600-h/playlist.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhWh2mymdeikIYNEF5tQ9etKdlbsN1tJpDqpyph1TKovoHyS8dwcEhBTY6ppNDdnd4Ls6kjhlGq8oXOLqWtFNfI2bpBR-hHWmk97V1tMtly-eWsmgZ5EjZr8Bd8xZ1rMdoPgL3fhOufZU4/s320/playlist.jpg" alt="" style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 243px;" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download Now Playing List &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/96/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;10. &lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;YABS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;YABS (Yet Another Black Songbird) is a polished feather that will perfectly complement a dark desktop theme.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg9EXk5Q0iwJLAp0OI4ryHZhdWS_ND9tonI-r7eb_vKL6xh1lctWIxcbfuQT4afV2tmRbGkPlcTrD1LIvj5-FNKHjt3dLEatT3kxeoDDsPp9lV_iRUx98OCXHBVVinyVUY0yMAiSS2K8BQ/s1600-h/YABS.jpg" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEg9EXk5Q0iwJLAp0OI4ryHZhdWS_ND9tonI-r7eb_vKL6xh1lctWIxcbfuQT4afV2tmRbGkPlcTrD1LIvj5-FNKHjt3dLEatT3kxeoDDsPp9lV_iRUx98OCXHBVVinyVUY0yMAiSS2K8BQ/s320/YABS.jpg" alt="" style="margin: 0px auto 10px; display: block; text-align: center; cursor: pointer; width: 320px; height: 192px;" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;Download YABS &lt;a href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/addon/1295/versions" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold;"&gt;HERE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;You can visit &lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;a style="font-weight: bold;" href="http://addons.songbirdnest.com/" target="Bwindow"&gt;HERE&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for the complete list of Songbird extensions. However, do take note that plenty of extensions that can be found there are still under development and may not be compatible with the latest version of &lt;a href="http://getsongbird.com/" target="Bwindow"&gt;Songbird&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;By the way, if you have other favorite Songbird add-ons that is not listed here, please share it with us via comment.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~a/SimplyJun?a=RxdpqR" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~a/SimplyJun?i=RxdpqR" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="feedflare"&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?a=dfg1O" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?i=dfg1O" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?a=86ZfO" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?i=86ZfO" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?a=RI4ZO" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?i=RI4ZO" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?a=Hjn0o" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?i=Hjn0o" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?a=BUBLo" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~f/SimplyJun?i=BUBLo" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/SimplyJun/~4/473700054" height="1" width="1" /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;/td&gt; &lt;td align="right" valign="top"&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;</description></item><item><title>In Car MP3 Player</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/in-car-mp3-player/</link><pubDate>Tue, 11 Nov 2008 08:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/in-car-mp3-player/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a onblur="try {parent.deselectBloggerImageGracefully();} catch(e) {}" href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh-r29fbP-Dofm1t9W_uLMO7GM1saBSta5s7iS_UN4ksNFEDax-4r9herjC2SuY_bGvHa5hY5DRcA3B_oYNXvNl8awKOx1Q7LLXt1ZFRXf8gRpmcGKrkhMSL2PGQaYvyDew6K2_vSHzZZM/s1600-h/DSC00489.JPG"&gt;&lt;img style="float:left; margin:0 10px 10px 0;cursor:pointer; cursor:hand;width: 299px; height: 400px;" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh-r29fbP-Dofm1t9W_uLMO7GM1saBSta5s7iS_UN4ksNFEDax-4r9herjC2SuY_bGvHa5hY5DRcA3B_oYNXvNl8awKOx1Q7LLXt1ZFRXf8gRpmcGKrkhMSL2PGQaYvyDew6K2_vSHzZZM/s400/DSC00489.JPG" border="0" alt="" id="BLOGGER_PHOTO_ID_5267307777629765042" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Got myself an in car MP3 player, you can either plug in the iPod etc or a USB drive or SD card with your tracks on it, which it then plays through the car&amp;rsquo;s radio.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/6fuord"&gt;In-Car 12v MP3 FM Modulator&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="http://tinyurl.com/5k3nwx"&gt;Memory2Go Orbit 360 2GB USB2.0 Flash Drive&lt;/a&gt; combined to make the drive to and from work more bearable.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Not bad for £17 including postage.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>MediaMonkey</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mediamonkey/</link><pubDate>Wed, 08 Oct 2008 08:26:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mediamonkey/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I found the intelligent tag editor really useful. &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;a name="base13329014"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a name="base13329014"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items13329014" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: FileHippo.com" href="http://www.filehippo.com/download_mediamonkey/4750/"&gt;MediaMonkey 3.0.5.1187&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;img style="float: left; margin-right: 5px;" src="http://i.filehippo.com/img/ex/1128__mediaMonkey2.gif" /&gt;MediaMonkey is a music manager and jukebox for serious music collectors and iPod users. It catalogs your CDs, OGG, WMA, MPC, FLAC, APE, WAV and MP3 audio files. It offers an intelligent tag editor which looks up missing Album Art and track information&amp;hellip;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="feedflare"&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/filehippo?a=PrTUM" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/filehippo?i=PrTUM" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/filehippo?a=SK2fm" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/filehippo?i=SK2fm" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;a href="http://www.filehippo.com/download_mediamonkey/"&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt; &lt;td align="right" valign="top"&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>VLC 0.9 Revamps Interface, Playlist Features [Featured Download]</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bloglines-vlc-09-revamps-interface/</link><pubDate>Mon, 29 Sep 2008 15:18:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bloglines-vlc-09-revamps-interface/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 17 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 21 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;One for the download list &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base1105048"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table1105048" bgcolor="#bde0ed" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;a href="http://lifehacker.com/"&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/base/img/thumbs140x140/lifehacker.com.png" alt="Lifehacker" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://lifehacker.com/"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Lifehacker&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Computers make us more productive. Yeah, right. Lifehacker recommends the software downloads and web sites that actually save time. Don&amp;rsquo;t live to geek; geek to live. &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base1105048"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items1105048" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Lifehacker" href="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Er/lifehacker/full/%7E3/406277252/vlc-09-revamps-interface-playlist-features"&gt;VLC 0.9 Revamps Interface, Playlist Features [Featured Download] &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; By Kevin Purdy on Windows &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/images/lifehacker/2008/09/vlc_new_interface.jpg" style="display: block; float: none;" align="left" height="215" hspace="4" vspace="2" width="494" /&gt;Windows/Mac/Linux: VLC 0.9.3, the bug-fixed, updated version of our favorite cross-platform, hardly-ever-fails media player, is available for download. New to this version are a revamped interface and reorganized menus, an improved playlist tool for more traditional audio-only file browsing and listening (and native playing of YouTube videos), enhanced album art and metadata tweaking, Last.fm submissions, and &lt;a href="http://wiki.videolan.org/What_is_cool_in_0.9/" target="Bwindow"&gt;much more&lt;/a&gt;. If you&amp;rsquo;ve already grabbed a new copy of VLC from an update, are you liking the new menus and interface, or are you tempted to switch back? Share your take in the comments. VLC Media Player 0.9.3 is a free download for Windows, Mac, and Linux systems (Windows downloads are currently 0.9.2).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="related"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.videolan.org/vlc/" target="Bwindow"&gt;VLC Media Player&lt;/a&gt; [via &lt;a href="http://www.linux.com/feature/148944" target="Bwindow"&gt;Linux.com&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/div&gt; &lt;img alt="" style="border: 0pt none ; height: 1px; width: 1px; display: none;" src="http://www.pheedo.com/img.phdo?i=508f9e7fad90befc1c126c47f838b356" border="0" height="1" width="1" /&gt;&lt;img src="http://www.pheedo.com/feeds/tracker.php?i=508f9e7fad90befc1c126c47f838b356" style="display: none;" alt="" border="0" height="1" width="1" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Ea/lifehacker/full?a=5lChOx" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.gawker.com/%7Ea/lifehacker/full?i=5lChOx" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Convert &amp;amp; Extract Audio from Videos</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/convert-extract-audio-from-videos/</link><pubDate>Sun, 28 Sep 2008 11:31:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/convert-extract-audio-from-videos/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 20 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 30 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Music from video &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;table id="table9477167" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="5" bg style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display:block; position:block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://feeds.cybernetnews.com/~r/CyberNet/~3/vGYOSP4FGcg/"&gt;Convert &amp;amp; Extract Audio from Videos&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feedads.googleadservices.com/~a/Tbj75J7Ci64pZWERl-vOKbilTNM/a"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feedads.googleadservices.com/~a/Tbj75J7Ci64pZWERl-vOKbilTNM/i" border="0" ismap="ismap" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/pazera.png" class="highslide"&gt;&lt;img src="http://cybernetnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/09/pazera-tm.jpg" width="450" height="337" alt="pazera.png" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Click to Enlarge)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;There have been a few times where I've wanted to extract audio from video files, but it's not always easy to find a free tool that can successfully do that. I highly recommend grabbing the &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.pazera-software.com/products/audio-extractor/"&gt;free Pazera app&lt;/a&gt; if you ever find yourself in a similar situation. To make it even more useful the program also doubles as an audio conversion utility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What are some things you can do with this? One great example is taking an FLV video (such as one from YouTube), and turning it into a standard MP3 music track. Think of all the free music you could get by doing this! It's important to note, however, that the audio quality of a YouTube video isn't exactly the greatest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here's a list of video and audio formats it supports during the conversion process, and also some great features you should know about:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video conversion&lt;/strong&gt;: AVI, DivX, XviD, MPEG, MPG, WMV, ASF, MOV, QT, FLV, SWF, MP4, M4V, 3GP, 3G2, RM, RMVB, MKV, VOB, VCD DAT, OGM, AMV to MP3, AAC, AC3, WMA, FLAC or WAV.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audio conversion&lt;/strong&gt;: WAV, MP3, AC3, AAC, M4A, MPC, MPA, MP2, WMA, FLAC, SHN, APE, OGG, WV, AMR to MP3, AAC, AC3, WMA, FLAC or WAV.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profiles&lt;/strong&gt;. Users can create custom profiles, or you can select from one of the many already available.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Doesn't need any installation&lt;/strong&gt;. Just extract ZIP archive and click AudioExtractor.exe file. All of the settings are stored in a single file so that it can be carried around with you!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;I guess if &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2006/10/13/super-is-the-ultimate-video-converter/"&gt;Super&lt;/a&gt; doesn't do the trick that this just might.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.pazera-software.com/products/audio-extractor/"&gt;Get Pazera&lt;/a&gt; [via &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://lifehacker.com/5054786/pazera-free-audio-extractor-rips-audio-from-any-video"&gt;Lifehacker&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Copyright © 2008 &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/"&gt;CyberNet&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://forum.cybernetnews.com/"&gt;CyberNet Forum&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://learnfirefox.cybernetnews.com/"&gt;Learn Firefox&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2008/09/26/convert-extract-audio-from-videos/"&gt;Convert &amp;amp; Extract Audio from Videos&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Related Posts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2007/05/02/cybernotes-converting-youtube-videos-to-avi-mpg-mp3-and-more-online/" title="Permanent Link: CyberNotes: Converting YouTube Videos to AVI, MPG, MP3, and More Online"&gt;CyberNotes: Converting YouTube Videos to AVI, MPG, MP3, and More Online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2006/12/28/cybernotes-how-to-convert-your-files-for-free-pdf-doc-etc/" title="Permanent Link: CyberNotes: How to Convert your Files for Free (PDF, DOC, etc…)"&gt;CyberNotes: How to Convert your Files for Free (PDF, DOC, etc…)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2006/10/13/super-is-the-ultimate-video-converter/" title="Permanent Link: Super Is the Ultimate Video Converter"&gt;Super Is the Ultimate Video Converter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2008/02/17/kmplayer-another-media-player/" title="Permanent Link: KMPlayer: Another Media Player"&gt;KMPlayer: Another Media Player&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://cybernetnews.com/2006/07/26/convert-firefox-bookmarks-feeds-to-ie7/" title="Permanent Link: Convert Firefox Bookmarks &amp;amp; Feeds To IE7"&gt;Convert Firefox Bookmarks &amp;amp; Feeds To IE7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class="feedflare"&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.cybernetnews.com/~f/CyberNet?a=Zu8Xfc1D"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feedproxy.google.com/~f/CyberNet?i=Zu8Xfc1D" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.cybernetnews.com/~f/CyberNet?a=rxFRGfC1"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feedproxy.google.com/~f/CyberNet?d=80" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.cybernetnews.com/~f/CyberNet?a=lC8mQSw3"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feedproxy.google.com/~f/CyberNet?i=lC8mQSw3" border=